{{!
    @template tool_openapi/documentation/viewer

    The interactive viewer. The container starts empty: the bundled Swagger
    UI fills it once it has fetched the document, which is why the page also
    loads tool_openapi/viewer.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * heading - Section heading
    * headingdesc - Sentence under the heading
    * tokenhint - What a reader needs before Try it out will work
    * backurl / backlabel - The way back to the documentation page
    * elementid - Id of the container Swagger UI renders into

    Example context (json):
    {
        "heading": "Interactive viewer",
        "headingdesc": "Browse every function this site exposes.",
        "tokenhint": "Paste a token into the wstoken field to send a request.",
        "backurl": "https://example.com/documentation/index.php",
        "backlabel": "Back to documentation",
        "elementid": "tool_openapi-viewer"
    }
}}
{{> tool_openapi/local/back_link}}

<h3>{{heading}}</h3>
<p class="text-muted">{{headingdesc}}</p>

<div class="alert alert-info" role="note">{{tokenhint}}</div>

<div id="{{elementid}}"></div>
